<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Masahiro SADAMURA</h1>

  <p>
    Researcher in legal psychology at the Graduate School of Human Sciences,
    The University of Osaka.
  </p>

  <p>
    He studies how Japanese criminal justice handles welfare-oriented
    information about defendants — developmental background, disability, and
    social isolation — in sentencing. His work combines vignette experiments
    with natural language processing of Japanese court decisions and explainable
    machine learning (SHAP). Recent work includes a
    <a href="/en/lab/r8-tanto">pre-registered public verification</a> of
    AI-derived answers to the Japanese bar examination.
  </p>

